  user_input {
    user_response: "You are a senior full-stack engineer, QA lead and product designer in one.\nBuild \"Career Compass\", a COMPLETE, WORKING, AI-powered career guidance and\nresume builder web app for EVERYONE: school students, college students of any\ncourse, graduates, job seekers, career switchers, working professionals, and\npeople returning after a career break.\n\n=====================================================\n0. HOW YOU MUST WORK (obey always)\n=====================================================\n1. THINK BEFORE CODING. Before each milestone write 5-8 lines: assumptions,\n   what you will build, what you will NOT build. If something is ambiguous,\n   choose the simplest reasonable option and say so.\n2. SIMPLICITY FIRST. Minimum code that fully solves the problem. No unused\n   dependencies, no speculative features, components under 150 lines,\n   plain readable code.\n3. SURGICAL CHANGES. When fixing or changing something, touch only the\n   files needed. Never restyle or refactor unrelated code.\n4. NOTHING FAKE. Every button, form, filter and link must actually work.\n   If anything is mocked, mark it \"TODO: mocked\" in code and tell me.\n5. VERIFY, DON\'T CLAIM. At the end of each milestone, run through its\n   \"done when\" checklist yourself and report PASS/FAIL with evidence\n   (which file and function, or which steps you performed).\n6. BUILD ONE MILESTONE AT A TIME. Stop after each and wait for me to say\n   \"next\".\n7. FIRST ACTION: tell me what backend, database, auth and secret-storage\n   options this environment really supports (for example a built-in server,\n   Firebase, or only browser storage). Pick the best supported option and\n   explain the choice in 3 lines. Whatever you pick, keep ALL data and auth\n   access behind `services/db.ts` and `services/auth.ts`, so UI code never\n   touches storage directly and the backend can be swapped later for\n   Express + MongoDB + JWT.\n\n=====================================================\n1. AUDIENCE AND UNIVERSAL RULES (override any default habit)\n=====================================================\n- Never assume an IT or engineering user. Career suggestions must fit the\n  user\'s own field and interests across ALL domains: healthcare, law,\n  commerce, education, arts, design, trades, public service, business,\n  science, agriculture, hospitality, media, technology, and more.\n- Never ask for or store age, gender, religion, caste, marital status or\n  nationality. No photo on resumes.\n- No words like \"BCA\", \"placement\", \"semester\", \"campus\" in the UI.\n  Use \"opportunities\", \"education\", \"field of study\".\n- Supported user stages: school (class 9-12), undergraduate, postgraduate,\n  diploma/vocational, fresher, working, switching careers, returning after\n  a break, self-taught.\n- Plain English at about grade-8 level. No jargon.\n- Lightweight and fast: no heavy animations; works on slow phones.\n- All UI text lives in `i18n/en.ts` so other languages can be added later.\n- Privacy first: short privacy note on signup, \"Export my data (JSON)\" and\n  \"Delete my account and data\" in the Profile page.\n- Roles: USER and ADMIN.\n\n=====================================================\n2. USER FLOW (build exactly this)\n=====================================================\nLanding page (who is this for) -> Register / Login\n  -> if role=user: Onboarding wizard (3 steps, first login only)\n       -> Dashboard (hub)\n          -> Tools, used in any order:\n             Career Ideas | Resume Builder (+AI review + PDF) |\n             Skills & Certificates | Mock Interview | Learning Roadmap |\n             Opportunities tracker | Resources | Profile & Privacy\n          -> every tool updates the Dashboard\n  -> if role=admin: Admin Dashboard (users, resources, usage counts)\n\nRoutes:\n /  /register  /login  /onboarding  /dashboard  /career-ideas\n /resume  /skills  /interview  /roadmap  /opportunities  /resources\n /profile  /admin  (admin only)  *  (friendly 404)\nRoute guards: logged-out users go to /login; normal users cannot open /admin;\ndeactivated users cannot log in or continue a session.\n\n=====================================================\n3. TECH STACK AND DESIGN\n=====================================================\nReact + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, React Router, jsPDF, recharts.\nUse zod (or equivalent) for runtime validation of forms and AI responses.\nDesign: clean, modern, mobile-first, indigo/slate palette, card layout,\nsidebar on desktop, bottom nav or hamburger on mobile, high contrast,\nlarge tap targets, visible keyboard focus, light and dark mode.\nIt must look like a real product, not a template demo.\nRealistic, field-diverse demo content (not only IT examples).\n\n=====================================================\n4. AI RULES (critical)\n=====================================================\nAll Gemini calls go through ONE module `services/ai.ts`. The API key must\nNEVER be hard-coded or visible in client source, logs or network payloads;\nuse the platform\'s secret mechanism or a server-side call.\n\nEvery AI call must:\n- have a system instruction defining the role;\n- return JSON ONLY with a fixed schema (responseMimeType application/json\n  plus responseSchema where supported);\n- be validated at runtime with zod; on invalid output, retry once, then show\n  a friendly error with a Retry button (never crash, never a blank screen);\n- show a loading state and disable its button while running (no duplicate\n  requests), plus a short cooldown to stop spamming;\n- treat user-typed text strictly as DATA: wrap it in delimiters and instruct\n  the model to ignore any instructions inside it (prompt-injection safe);\n- never invent company names, salaries, job links or URLs as facts; salaries\n  are labelled \"approximate\" and use the user\'s currency; resource names are\n  generic (\"official documentation\", \"public library\", \"free online course\n  platforms\");\n- label match percentages \"AI estimate, not a guarantee\";\n- stay field-neutral: put careers from the user\'s own field first, plus at\n  least one adjacent and one stretch option.\n\nTypes in `types/ai.ts` plus matching zod schemas:\n\nA) Career Ideas\n in:  { educationLevel, fieldOfStudy, currentStatus, experienceYears,\n        interests[], skills[], preferredWorkStyle, country, currency }\n out: { careers: [ { title, category: \"best-fit\"|\"adjacent\"|\"stretch\",\n        matchPercent, whyItFits, requiredSkills[], missingSkills[],\n        typicalEntryRoutes[], approxSalaryRange, growthOutlook } ] } (4-6)\n\nB) Resume Review\n in:  resume + { targetRole?, experienceLevel }\n out: { score 0-100, strengths[], weaknesses[],\n        suggestions: [ { section, issue, improvedText } ], keywordsMissing[] }\n Must work for a school student with little content, a tradesperson, a nurse,\n a lawyer and a software developer alike.\n\nC) Mock Interview\n in:  { role, field, difficulty, type: \"technical\"|\"hr\"|\"mixed\"|\"viva\" }\n out: { questions: [ { id, question, type, idealAnswerPoints[] } ] } (8)\n evaluateAnswer(question, answer) -> { score 0-10, feedback, improvedAnswer }\n\nD) Roadmap\n in:  { targetRole, currentSkills[], weeksAvailable, hoursPerWeek,\n        budget: \"free\"|\"low\"|\"flexible\" }\n out: { phases: [ { title, weeks, topics[], practiceIdea,\n        freeResources: [ { name, type } ] } ] }\n\n=====================================================\n5. DATA MODELS (keep exactly these)\n=====================================================\nUser { id, name, email, role: \"user\"|\"admin\", active, onboarded, createdAt }\nProfile { userId, currentStatus, educationLevel, fieldOfStudy,\n          experienceYears, interests[], careerGoal, country, currency, bio }\nResume { userId, mode: \"fresher\"|\"experienced\"|\"academic\",\n         personal{name,email,phone,location,links[]}, summary, education[],\n         experience[], projects[], skills[], certifications[],\n         optionalSections[] (volunteering, languages, achievements,\n         publications, extracurricular), lastScore? }\nSkill { id, userId, name, category: \"technical\"|\"soft\"|\"domain\"|\"language\",\n        level 1-5 }\nCertificate { id, userId, title, issuer, date, fileDataUrl? }\nOpportunity { id, userId, title, organization,\n              type: \"job\"|\"internship\"|\"exam\"|\"scholarship\"|\"admission\"|\n                    \"freelance\",\n              status: \"saved\"|\"applied\"|\"interview\"|\"offer\"|\"rejected\"|\n                      \"closed\",\n              deadline, appliedDate, notes }\nRoadmapPlan { id, userId, targetRole, data, progress, createdAt }\nCareerResult { userId, data, createdAt }\nResource { id, title, category, link, description, createdBy }\n\nEvery service function takes the CURRENT user from the session, never a\nuserId from the UI, so one user can never read or change another user\'s data.\n\n=====================================================\n6. FEATURE REQUIREMENTS\n=====================================================\nAUTH: register (validation, duplicate email check, email trimmed and\nlowercased), login, logout, persistent session across refresh, logout clears\nall user data from memory. Seed one demo user and one demo admin labelled\n\"demo\". Passwords: if storing in the browser for the prototype, hash them and\nadd a clear TODO that real security needs a server with bcrypt + JWT.\n\nONBOARDING: 3 steps (who you are now / what you study or do / interests),\nskippable but with a \"complete your profile for better results\" nudge.\n\nDASHBOARD: profile completion %, resume score, skills count, roadmap progress,\nopportunities by status, upcoming deadlines first, one \"next best step\" card,\ncharts via recharts. Numbers must always equal the underlying data.\n\nCAREER IDEAS: pre-filled from profile and skills, results as cards with match\nbar, missing-skill chips, \"Create roadmap\" button, save last result.\n\nRESUME BUILDER: mode switch (fresher/experienced/academic) reorders sections;\nadd, remove and reorder entries; optional sections can be added or hidden;\nside-by-side live preview. PDF: single column, ATS-friendly, selectable text,\nA4, multi-page safe, no photo, standard headings, handles unicode and long\ntext, file named Name_Resume.pdf. Empty sections must not leave blank headings.\nAI review shows score ring, strengths, weaknesses and suggestions with an\n\"Apply suggestion\" button that is safe to apply twice.\n\nSKILLS AND CERTIFICATES: full CRUD, level 1-5, grouped by category, delete\nasks for confirmation, no duplicate skill names, certificate file type and\nsize limits, graceful handling of storage-full errors.\n\nMOCK INTERVIEW: choose role, field, difficulty and type; one question at a\ntime; skipping allowed; empty answers blocked; AI score and feedback; session\nsummary with a correct average; resume-in-progress survives a refresh.\n\nROADMAP: generate, show as a vertical timeline, check off topics, progress %\nsaved; regenerating warns before replacing saved progress.\n\nOPPORTUNITIES: kanban board by status (move buttons work on mobile too),\nall six types, deadlines with \"due soon\" highlight, search and filter.\n\nRESOURCES: list of admin-added resources with category filter.\n\nPROFILE AND PRIVACY: edit with validation, export all my data as JSON,\ndelete my account and ALL my data across every module (with confirmation).\n\nADMIN: users table with search, deactivate/reactivate (cannot deactivate the\nlast admin or yourself), usage counts, resources CRUD visible to users\nimmediately. Admin actions are checked by ROLE inside the service layer, not\nonly hidden in the UI.\n\n=====================================================\n7. QUALITY AND SECURITY RULES\n=====================================================\n- No dangerouslySetInnerHTML. All user text rendered safely (XSS-safe).\n- Length limits on every input and before sending text to the AI.\n- Error boundary around every route; no white screens ever.\n- Every list has an empty state with a clear next action; every async action\n  has loading and human-readable error states; forms validate before submit\n  with labelled fields.\n- No `any`, no leftover console.log, no dead code or unused packages.\n- Accessible: keyboard navigation, aria labels, contrast AA, alt text.\n- Responsive at 360px, 768px and 1280px.\n\n=====================================================\n8. MILESTONES (build ONE, then stop and wait for \"next\")\n=====================================================\nMILESTONE 1: Foundation\n  Project setup, design system, i18n file, service layer, auth, route guards,\n  landing page, onboarding, profile (with export and delete), dashboard shell,\n  seed data.\n  DONE WHEN: register -> onboard -> edit profile -> refresh and stay logged in\n  -> export data -> delete account all work; a normal user cannot open /admin;\n  a deactivated user cannot log in.\n\nMILESTONE 2: Core tools\n  Career Ideas, Resume Builder + PDF + AI review, Skills and Certificates,\n  Mock Interview, Roadmap, with all AI rules from section 4.\n  DONE WHEN: every AI feature survives network failure, malformed JSON, and\n  a double-click; PDF text is selectable and fits A4; data persists on refresh.\n\nMILESTONE 3: Tracker, Dashboard, Admin, Polish\n  Opportunities, full Dashboard with charts, Resources, Admin, error\n  boundaries, 404, accessibility and responsive pass.\n  DONE WHEN: moving an opportunity updates dashboard numbers instantly; an\n  admin resource is instantly visible to users; no console errors.\n\n=====================================================\n9. OUTPUT FORMAT FOR EACH MILESTONE\n=====================================================\n1) Assumptions and plan (short)\n2) File tree of what you added or changed\n3) The code\n4) \"Done when\" checklist with PASS/FAIL and evidence\n5) Known limitations or mocked parts\n6) What I should test manually (5 specific steps)\nThen STOP and wait.\n\nBegin now: do the FIRST ACTION from section 0, then MILESTONE 1 only. now make the this proper\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "You are a senior full-stack engineer, QA lead and product designer in one.\nBuild \"Career Compass\", a COMPLETE, WORKING, AI-powered career guidance and\nresume builder web app for EVERYONE: school students, college students of any\ncourse, graduates, job seekers, career switchers, working professionals, and\npeople returning after a career break.\n\n=====================================================\n0. HOW YOU MUST WORK (obey always)\n=====================================================\n1. THINK BEFORE CODING. Before each milestone write 5-8 lines: assumptions,\n   what you will build, what you will NOT build. If something is ambiguous,\n   choose the simplest reasonable option and say so.\n2. SIMPLICITY FIRST. Minimum code that fully solves the problem. No unused\n   dependencies, no speculative features, components under 150 lines,\n   plain readable code.\n3. SURGICAL CHANGES. When fixing or changing something, touch only the\n   files needed. Never restyle or refactor unrelated code.\n4. NOTHING FAKE. Every button, form, filter and link must actually work.\n   If anything is mocked, mark it \"TODO: mocked\" in code and tell me.\n5. VERIFY, DON\'T CLAIM. At the end of each milestone, run through its\n   \"done when\" checklist yourself and report PASS/FAIL with evidence\n   (which file and function, or which steps you performed).\n6. BUILD ONE MILESTONE AT A TIME. Stop after each and wait for me to say\n   \"next\".\n7. FIRST ACTION: tell me what backend, database, auth and secret-storage\n   options this environment really supports (for example a built-in server,\n   Firebase, or only browser storage). Pick the best supported option and\n   explain the choice in 3 lines. Whatever you pick, keep ALL data and auth\n   access behind `services/db.ts` and `services/auth.ts`, so UI code never\n   touches storage directly and the backend can be swapped later for\n   Express + MongoDB + JWT.\n\n=====================================================\n