  planner_response {
    response: "### First Action \342\200\224 Environment Capabilities & Architecture Choice (Section 0.7)\n\n1. **What this environment supports**: A full-stack Node.js + Express backend (`server.ts` on port 3000) with server-side secret injection (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`), browser storage (`localStorage`), and optional cloud provisioning (Firebase / Cloud SQL).\n2. **Selected architecture**: We use the **Express server proxy (`server.ts`)** for all `@google/genai` (`gemini-3-flash-preview`) calls so `GEMINI_API_KEY` stays strictly server-side, paired with a **session-scoped service layer (`src/services/auth.ts` and `src/services/db.ts`)** backed by structured `localStorage` (`cc_*_v2`) for immediate zero-config reliability.\n3. **Drop-in backend swap guarantee**: UI components never touch `localStorage` or pass `userId` parameters; every function in `services/db.ts` resolves the active user from the session (`requireSessionUser()`), making a future swap to Express + MongoDB + JWT a single-file service replacement.\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 1 \342\200\224 Foundation (`types`, `i18n/en.ts`, `services/auth.ts`, `services/db.ts`, Layout, Onboarding, Profile & Privacy, Routing & Guards)\n\n#### 1) Assumptions and Plan (5\342\200\2238 lines)\n- **Assumptions**: Career Compass serves learners and job seekers across **all fields** (healthcare, commerce, arts, law, skilled trades, education, science, and software). The default demo account (`demo@careercompass.org` / `demo123`) is seeded with a Full-Stack Development profile in **India (`INR`)**, while a global country/currency selector (`INR`, `USD`, `GBP`, `EUR`, `CAD`, `AUD`, `SGD`) is available to all users.\n- **What we built in Milestone 1**: Strict TypeScript models and Zod schemas (`src/types/index.ts`, `src/types/ai.ts`), centralized plain-English copy (`src/i18n/en.ts`), session-scoped auth & storage services (`src/services/auth.ts`, `src/services/db.ts`), responsive `Navbar` + `Sidebar` + `AppShell` with Light/Dark mode toggle, a 3-step `/onboarding` wizard, `/profile` editor with **Export My Data (JSON)** and **Delete My Account**, and `ProtectedRoute` role/status guards with a dedicated `NotFoundPage`.\n- **What we did NOT build as new scope in Milestone 1**: No OAuth/social login, no email verification server, and no external MongoDB connection yet (all data operations are encapsulated in `services/db.ts` and `services/auth.ts`).\n\n#### 2) File Tree Added / Changed\n```text\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.html\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 metadata.json\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.css\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 i18n/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 en.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ai.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 auth.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 db.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ai.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 context/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AuthContext.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 auth/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProtectedRoute.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 layout/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AppShell.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Navbar.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Sidebar.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 resume/\n    \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResumeLivePreview.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LandingPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LoginPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 RegisterPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 OnboardingPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfilePage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 NotFoundPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 RecommendationsPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResumePage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SkillsPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 InterviewPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 RoadmapPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 TrackerPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResourcesPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AdminPage.tsx\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 pdfExport.ts\n```\n\n#### 3) Key Code Highlights\n- **Session-Scoped Data Isolation (`src/services/db.ts`)**:\n  - `getProfile()`, `saveProfile(input)`, `listSkills()`, `saveSkill(input)`, `exportMyDataAsJson()`, and `deleteMyAccountAndAllData()` all call `await requireSessionUser()` internally instead of accepting a `userId` from UI components.\n- **Active Account & Onboarding Enforcement (`src/services/auth.ts` & `src/components/auth/ProtectedRoute.tsx`)**:\n  - `getCurrentUser()` and `requireSessionUser()` re-verify the stored user record on every call; if an admin sets `active: false`, the session is immediately cleared.\n  - `ProtectedRoute` redirects any authenticated user with `onboarded === false` to `/onboarding`, blocks non-admin users from `/admin` with an explicit 403 screen, and preserves deep links on login.\n- **Privacy Controls (`src/services/db.ts` & `src/pages/ProfilePage.tsx`)**:\n  - `exportMyDataAsJson()` bundles the user\'s account, profile, skills, certificates, resume, career ideas, roadmap, and opportunities into a downloadable JSON file.\n  - `deleteMyAccountAndAllData()` purges every collection entry belonging to the current user and deletes their account record.\n\n#### 4) Milestone 1 \"Done When\" Checklist (Verified)\n- **[PASS] Register -> Onboard -> Edit Profile -> Refresh and stay logged in**:\n  - *Evidence*: `registerUser()` (`src/services/auth.ts:112`) creates a user with `onboarded: false`; `ProtectedRoute` (`src/components/auth/ProtectedRoute.tsx:31`) routes to `OnboardingPage.tsx`, which calls `saveProfile()` + `completeOnboarding()` (`src/pages/OnboardingPage.tsx:78-92`). `AuthContext` (`src/context/AuthContext.tsx:36`) restores the session on page reload via `getCurrentUser()`.\n- **[PASS] Export My Data (JSON) & Delete My Account and All Data work**:\n  - *Evidence*: `handleExportData()` and `handleDeleteAccount()` in `src/pages/ProfilePage.tsx:120-154` invoke `exportMyDataAsJson()` (`src/services/db.ts:520`) and `deleteMyAccountAndAllData()` (`src/services/db.ts:548`).\n- **[PASS] Normal user cannot open `/admin`**:\n  - *Evidence*: `/admin` is wrapped in `<ProtectedRoute allowedRole=\"admin\">` (`src/App.tsx:136`), which renders an Access Denied (403) view when `user.role !== \'admin\'` (`src/components/auth/ProtectedRoute.tsx:36-62`). Additionally, `listUsers()`, `toggleUserActiveStatus()`, `saveResource()`, `deleteResource()`, and `getPlatformStats()` enforce `actor.role === \'admin\'` inside the service layer.\n- **[PASS] Deactivated user cannot log in or continue an active session**:\n  - *Evidence*: `loginUser()` (`src/services/auth.ts:154`) rejects deactivated accounts with `\"This account has been deactivated by an administrator.\"`, and `getCurrentUser()` (`src/services/auth.ts:176`) clears `SESSION_KEY` if `found.active === false`.\n- **[PASS] Zero banned words (`\"BCA\"`, `\"placement\"`, `\"semester\"`, `\"campus\"`), zero `any`, zero `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, and clean build**:\n  - *Evidence*: Verified via `grep -rnE -i \'bca|placement|semester|campus|dangerouslySetInnerHTML\'` (`0` matches), `tsc --noEmit` (`0` errors), and `vite build` (`Build succeeded`).\n\n#### 5) Known Limitations / Mocked Parts\n- **Client-Side Auth & Storage Prototype (`// TODO: mocked` in `src/services/auth.ts:12`)**:\n  - User records, SHA-256 password hashes (`hashPasswordClientSide`), and domain collections currently persist in browser `localStorage` (`cc_*_v2`) so the app runs self-contained in preview. Moving to production only requires swapping the implementations inside `src/services/auth.ts` and `src/services/db.ts` to call Express + MongoDB + HTTP-only JWT endpoints.\n\n#### 6) What You Should Test Manually (5 Steps)\n1. **New User Registration & 2-Minute Onboarding**: Click **Get Started** -> register a new account -> verify you are automatically redirected to `/onboarding` -> complete the 3 steps (Stage, Field & Country/Currency, Interests & Goal) and click **Finish Setup**.\n2. **Profile Validation, Persistence & Dark Mode**: Go to **Profile** (`/profile`), add a new interest tag, update your career goal, toggle **Dark Mode** in the top navbar, and refresh the browser tab to confirm both your session and dark theme persist.\n3. **Role Guard on `/admin`**: While logged in as a regular user (or the demo user `demo@careercompass.org`), navigate to `/admin` and verify the 403 Access Restricted screen blocks access.\n4. **Admin Deactivation Enforcement**: Log out, click the **Demo Admin** quick-login button on `/login`, open `/admin`, deactivate the user account you created, then try logging back into that deactivated account to confirm login is blocked.\n5. **Privacy Export & Account Deletion**: Log in with a test account, open `/profile`, click **Export My Data (JSON)** to download your JSON archive, and then click **Delete My Account** to confirm your data and session are wiped and you are returned to `/login`.\n\n---\n**Stopped after Milestone 1.** Reply **`\"next\"`** when you are ready to proceed to **Milestone 2**."
    modified_response: "### First Action \342\200\224 Environment Capabilities & Architecture Choice (Section 0.7)\n\n1. **What this environment supports**: A full-stack Node.js + Express backend (`server.ts` on port 3000) with server-side secret injection (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`), browser storage (`localStorage`), and optional cloud provisioning (Firebase / Cloud SQL).\n2. **Selected architecture**: We use the **Express server proxy (`server.ts`)** for all `@google/genai` (`gemini-3-flash-preview`) calls so `GEMINI_API_KEY` stays strictly server-side, paired with a **session-scoped service layer (`src/services/auth.ts` and `src/services/db.ts`)** backed by structured `localStorage` (`cc_*_v2`) for immediate zero-config reliability.\n3. **Drop-in backend swap guarantee**: UI components never touch `localStorage` or pass `userId` parameters; every function in `services/db.ts` resolves the active user from the session (`requireSessionUser()`), making a future swap to Express + MongoDB + JWT a single-file service replacement.\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 1 \342\200\224 Foundation (`types`, `i18n/en.ts`, `services/auth.ts`, `services/db.ts`, Layout, Onboarding, Profile & Privacy, Routing & Guards)\n\n#### 1) Assumptions and Plan (5\342\200\2238 lines)\n- **Assumptions**: Career Compass serves learners and job seekers across **all fields** (healthcare, commerce, arts, law, skilled trades, education, science, and software). The default demo account (`demo@careercompass.org` / `demo123`) is seeded with a Full-Stack Development profile in **India (`INR`)**, while a global country/currency selector (`INR`, `USD`, `GBP`, `EUR`, `CAD`, `AUD`, `SGD`) is available to all users.\n- **What we built in Milestone 1**: Strict TypeScript models and Zod schemas (`src/types/index.ts`, `src/types/ai.ts`), centralized plain-English copy (`src/i18n/en.ts`), session-scoped auth & storage services (`src/services/auth.ts`, `src/services/db.ts`), responsive `Navbar` + `Sidebar` + `AppShell` with Light/Dark mode toggle, a 3-step `/onboarding` wizard, `/profile` editor with **Export My Data (JSON)** and **Delete My Account**, and `ProtectedRoute` role/status guards with a dedicated `NotFoundPage`.\n- **What we did NOT build as new scope in Milestone 1**: No OAuth/social login, no email verification server, and no external MongoDB connection yet (all data operations are encapsulated in `services/db.ts` and `services/auth.ts`).\n\n#### 2) File Tree Added / Changed\n```text\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.html\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 metadata.json\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.css\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 i18n/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 en.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ai.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 auth.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 db.ts\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ai.ts\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 context/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AuthContext.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 auth/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProtectedRoute.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 layout/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 AppShell.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Navbar.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Sidebar.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 resume/\n    \342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResumeLivePreview.tsx\n    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 pages/\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LandingPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 LoginPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 RegisterPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 OnboardingPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ProfilePage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 NotFoundPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 DashboardPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 RecommendationsPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResumePage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 SkillsPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 InterviewPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 RoadmapPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 TrackerPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 ResourcesPage.tsx\n    \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 AdminPage.tsx\n    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/\n        \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 pdfExport.ts\n```\n\n#### 3) Key Code Highlights\n- **Session-Scoped Data Isolation (`src/services/db.ts`)**:\n  - `getProfile()`, `saveProfile(input)`, `listSkills()`, `saveSkill(input)`, `exportMyDataAsJson()`, and `deleteMyAccountAndAllData()` all call `await requireSessionUser()` internally instead of accepting a `userId` from UI components.\n- **Active Account & Onboarding Enforcement (`src/services/auth.ts` & `src/components/auth/ProtectedRoute.tsx`)**:\n  - `getCurrentUser()` and `requireSessionUser()` re-verify the stored user record on every call; if an admin sets `active: false`, the session is immediately cleared.\n  - `ProtectedRoute` redirects any authenticated user with `onboarded === false` to `/onboarding`, blocks non-admin users from `/admin` with an explicit 403 screen, and preserves deep links on login.\n- **Privacy Controls (`src/services/db.ts` & `src/pages/ProfilePage.tsx`)**:\n  - `exportMyDataAsJson()` bundles the user\'s account, profile, skills, certificates, resume, career ideas, roadmap, and opportunities into a downloadable JSON file.\n  - `deleteMyAccountAndAllData()` purges every collection entry belonging to the current user and deletes their account record.\n\n#### 4) Milestone 1 \"Done When\" Checklist (Verified)\n- **[PASS] Register -> Onboard -> Edit Profile -> Refresh and stay logged in**:\n  - *Evidence*: `registerUser()` (`src/services/auth.ts:112`) creates a user with `onboarded: false`; `ProtectedRoute` (`src/components/auth/ProtectedRoute.tsx:31`) routes to `OnboardingPage.tsx`, which calls `saveProfile()` + `completeOnboarding()` (`src/pages/OnboardingPage.tsx:78-92`). `AuthContext` (`src/context/AuthContext.tsx:36`) restores the session on page reload via `getCurrentUser()`.\n- **[PASS] Export My Data (JSON) & Delete My Account and All Data work**:\n  - *Evidence*: `handleExportData()` and `handleDeleteAccount()` in `src/pages/ProfilePage.tsx:120-154` invoke `exportMyDataAsJson()` (`src/services/db.ts:520`) and `deleteMyAccountAndAllData()` (`src/services/db.ts:548`).\n- **[PASS] Normal user cannot open `/admin`**:\n  - *Evidence*: `/admin` is wrapped in `<ProtectedRoute allowedRole=\"admin\">` (`src/App.tsx:136`), which renders an Access Denied (403) view when `user.role !== \'admin\'` (`src/components/auth/ProtectedRoute.tsx:36-62`). Additionally, `listUsers()`, `toggleUserActiveStatus()`, `saveResource()`, `deleteResource()`, and `getPlatformStats()` enforce `actor.role === \'admin\'` inside the service layer.\n- **[PASS] Deactivated user cannot log in or continue an active session**:\n  - *Evidence*: `loginUser()` (`src/services/auth.ts:154`) rejects deactivated accounts with `\"This account has been deactivated by an administrator.\"`, and `getCurrentUser()` (`src/services/auth.ts:176`) clears `SESSION_KEY` if `found.active === false`.\n- **[PASS] Zero banned words (`\"BCA\"`, `\"placement\"`, `\"semester\"`, `\"campus\"`), zero `any`, zero `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, and clean build**:\n  - *Evidence*: Verified via `grep -rnE -i \'bca|placement|semester|campus|dangerouslySetInnerHTML\'` (`0` matches), `tsc --noEmit` (`0` errors), and `vite build` (`Build succeeded`).\n\n#### 5) Known Limitations / Mocked Parts\n- **Client-Side Auth & Storage Prototype (`// TODO: mocked` in `src/services/auth.ts:12`)**:\n  - User records, SHA-256 password hashes (`hashPasswordClientSide`), and domain collections currently persist in browser `localStorage` (`cc_*_v2`) so the app runs self-contained in preview. Moving to production only requires swapping the implementations inside `src/services/auth.ts` and `src/services/db.ts` to call Express + MongoDB + HTTP-only JWT endpoints.\n\n#### 6) What You Should Test Manually (5 Steps)\n1. **New User Registration & 2-Minute Onboarding**: Click **Get Started** -> register a new account -> verify you are automatically redirected to `/onboarding` -> complete the 3 steps (Stage, Field & Country/Currency, Interests & Goal) and click **Finish Setup**.\n2. **Profile Validation, Persistence & Dark Mode**: Go to **Profile** (`/profile`), add a new interest tag, update your career goal, toggle **Dark Mode** in the top navbar, and refresh the browser tab to confirm both your session and dark theme persist.\n3. **Role Guard on `/admin`**: While logged in as a regular user (or the demo user `demo@careercompass.org`), navigate to `/admin` and verify the 403 Access Restricted screen blocks access.\n4. **Admin Deactivation Enforcement**: Log out, click the **Demo Admin** quick-login button on `/login`, open `/admin`, deactivate the user account you created, then try logging back into that deactivated account to confirm login is blocked.\n5. **Privacy Export & Account Deletion**: Log in with a test account, open `/profile`, click **Export My Data (JSON)** to download your JSON archive, and then click **Delete My Account** to confirm your data and session are wiped and you are returned to `/login`.\n\n---\n**Stopped after Milestone 1.** Reply **`\"next\"`** when you are ready to proceed to **Milestone 2**."
